var WPA={"Brigandine":{"o":{"ac":13,"dex":"full","cat":"Light","w":25,"dis":1},"c":50.0,"t":"A thick coat reaching just below the waist, made of heavy cloth or canvas lined inside with small metal plates. Lighter sleeveless versions are popular with nobles at court, but use leather armor's statistics and protect only the upper body."},"Silk-Backed Coin Mail":{"o":{"ac":14,"dex":"max2","cat":"Medium","w":50,"dis":1},"c":2000.0,"t":"A hauberk of silver coins from conquered nations backed by quilted red wormsilk, usually awarded to soldiers, mercenaries and generals of conspicuous valor in the campaign that took the coins' homeland. While wearing it, you have Resistance to Piercing damage from nonmagical weapons. If the Piercing damage is from a critical hit, the armor loses this property until you spend a short rest repairing it, with no tools or check needed."},"Stonesteel":{"o":{"ac":19,"dex":"none","cat":"Heavy","w":80,"str":16,"dis":1},"c":3000.0,"t":"An alloy of steel and crystalline stone, and the height of dwarven metalwork. Overlapping, interlocking plates cover the whole body, with gauntlets, heavy leather boots and a helmet. It is heavy and somewhat clumsy but protects better than standard plate. Donning or doffing it takes twice as long as normal plate."}};
